{
  "$comment": [
    "The Gearbox 1.0 ABI surface, frozen. NOT a copy of abi.json -- only the",
    "three things a COMPILED mod depends on: the import name, its wire",
    "signature, and the capability that gates it. Docs and parameter names may",
    "be reworded freely; those cannot break a .wasm that already exists.",
    "",
    "tools/check_abi_compat.py asserts every entry here is still present and",
    "unchanged in sdk/abi.json. That is what makes \"a 1.0 mod keeps working\" a",
    "tested guarantee rather than an intention: within major version 1, a",
    "symbol may be added but never renamed, re-signed, or re-gated.",
    "",
    "A genuinely incompatible change means Gearbox 2.0, a new baseline file,",
    "and mods that declare it -- parseModManifest already refuses a mismatched",
    "major outright."
  ],
